From f9fdb6090cf9dbf212979cf8ceee51e5ee31f236 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:05:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tier 0: measuring takes selection's list and sums positions
 in its words' loop (#2874)

Measuring listed the deferred entries again in its loop over the words,
counted them in a second loop, and summed the lengths into positions in
a third. In a function without deep entries the list is selection's:
only tier0_select_deep defers an entry after selection, and a template's
case word is never deferred. Selection now keeps its list's count
(Tier0Entries.deferred_count), measuring counts those entries first
(tier0_measure_listed), and the words' loop takes a deferred lane's
length from that loop and each block's positions as the prefix sums of
its lengths from a carry. A function with deep entries lists, counts and
sums as before. The table of calls fills in the same order: the list's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EgbxngDHhCG4YpQkQHQURG
Signed-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>
